# n8n MCP Skill

**Server:** n8n-mcp  
**Transport:** stdio (npx -y n8n-mcp)  
**Config:** N8N_API_URL, N8N_API_KEY (env)

## When to use

- Triggering or querying n8n workflows from Cursor/agent
- Listing workflows, executions, or nodes
- Integrating n8n automation into development or ops tasks
- Any "run n8n workflow" or "check n8n execution" task

## Usage

Reference this skill with `@mcp-skills/n8n-mcp` when you need to interact with n8n. Use exact tool names from the MCP server; API URL and key are set in Cursor MCP env.

## Notes

- Server runs via npx; ensure Node/npx available where Cursor runs.
- Do not hardcode N8N_API_KEY in project code; keep in MCP env only.
